---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Island from '../components/Island.astro';
import {product} from '../data/site';
import {release} from '../data/release';
---
<Layout title="Floatlet | Free Dynamic Island for Windows 11">
<section class="hero wrap"><div class="hero-kicker"><span class="windows-icon" aria-hidden="true">⊞</span> A NATIVE COMPANION FOR WINDOWS 11</div><h1>A little island.<br/><span>A calmer desktop.</span></h1><div class="hero-bottom"><p>Music, files, and useful controls.<br/>Right there when you need them.<br/>Quietly out of the way when you don't.</p><div class="hero-actions"><a class="button primary" href={release?.url||product.repository+'/releases'} data-event="download_click" data-placement="hero">Download for Windows <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="underlink" href="#experience">Try the island ↘</a><a class="underlink" href={product.repository} data-event="github_click">GitHub ↗</a><span class="fine">Free & open source · x64 preview · Unsigned</span></div></div></section>
<section class="experience wrap" id="experience" aria-label="Try Floatlet"><Island/></section>
<section class="intro wrap"><p class="eyebrow">LESS SWITCHING. MORE DOING.</p><h2>The small things,<br/>a little closer.</h2><p>Skip a track. Keep a file handy. Turn the volume down. Floatlet brings everyday actions into one small surface, inspired by the Dynamic Island concept and built for Windows.</p></section>
<section class="story wrap" aria-label="Explore the island"><div class="story-rail"><span class="eyebrow">ONE LITTLE SPACE</span><h2>Room for<br/>your rhythm.</h2><a class="underlink" href="#experience">Back to the live preview ↑</a></div><div class="story-chapters"><article id="music"><span class="chapter-no">01 / MUSIC</span><h3>Keep the song.<br/>Lose the detour.</h3><p>Album artwork and playback controls from supported Windows media sessions. Hover for the next track, without hunting for your player.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="music">Try music controls ↗</button></article><article id="files"><span class="chapter-no">02 / TRAY</span><h3>A stop along<br/>the way.</h3><p>Drop a file reference into the tray, then drag it into another app when you're ready. Removing a reference leaves your original file untouched.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="files">Try the sample tray ↗</button></article><article id="controls"><span class="chapter-no">03 / CONTROLS</span><h3>Small adjustments.<br/>No big interruption.</h3><p>Volume, supported display brightness and nearby Wi-Fi. A timer when you need a moment. A calendar when you need to look ahead.</p><button class="chapter-button" data-chapter="controls">Try the controls ↗</button></article></div></section>
<section class="honest wrap"><div><p class="eyebrow">NATIVE BY DESIGN</p><h2>A small surface.<br/>An open project.</h2></div><div><p>Built with C++ and Windows composition. No bundled browser. No account required for the app.</p><p class="muted">This is an early preview. Some controls open Windows settings. Battery savings and 120 Hz smoothness have not been verified.</p><a class="underlink" href="/docs/capabilities/">What works, and what doesn't ↗</a></div></section>
<section class="evidence wrap"><p class="eyebrow">THE REAL APP</p><h2>Source you can inspect.</h2><p>The demo above uses sample content. Approved native screenshots and a recording are still being prepared. Until then, inspect the code, release notes and test evidence directly.</p><a class="underlink" href={product.repository} data-event="github_click">Explore the repository ↗</a></section>
<section class="get-it"><div class="wrap"><span class="eyebrow">MAKE A LITTLE ROOM</span><h2>Your desktop.<br/>With Floatlet.</h2><a class="button primary" href="/download/">Get the Windows preview ↓</a><p>Free. MIT licensed. Yours to explore.</p></div></section></Layout>
